    "https://jobs.tufts.edu/jobs/22721?lang=en-us": {
      "title": "System Administrator in Medford, Massachusetts",
      "description": "System Administrator in Medford, Massachusetts | Tufts University Skip to Main Content toggle menu CLOSE About Benefits Opportunities DEI Community Open Positions Back System Administrator JOB_DESCRIPTION.SHARE.HTML CAROUSEL_PARAGRAPH JOB_DESCRIPTION.SHARE.HTML Medford, Massachusetts On-Site (IT) Information Technology 22721 mail_outline Get future jobs matching this search Login or Register Job Description Overview Provide technical support for Microsoft Windows and Apple OSX in several different environments including virtualized systems, servers, workstations, and laptops.  Locally and remotely provision and deploy systems in an unattended manner using a combination of vendor provided tools, third party software and custom scripts. Automate repetitive systems administration tasks such as user account management and network configuration. Working as part of a team, candidate also serves as first line of support for faculty, staff, and students. What You'll Do Manage Windows servers.  This includes managing users and security with Active Directory and managing the infrastructure that supports automated system provisioning for several hundred desktop systems. Provide end-to-end Windows and Apple desktop support for the user community for routine requests such as software installs, managing system security settings, and replacing failed hardware. Support “core” services provided by the systems group including printing, account management, quota management, performing security audits, and regularly updating workflow documentation. Assist users both locally and remotely with regular Linux based requests such as quota increases, password resets, and automated OS installation. Resolve user-related problems as appropriate.  Other duties as assigned. This role requires ongoing coordination with Tufts Technology Services where the incumbent must adhere to established data governance policies, technology standards, and system administration best practices as defined by TTS. This includes use of approved platforms and tools, participation in IT security protocols and periodic technical planning efforts for related systems, as well as alignment with enterprise-wide technology initiatives and strategies. What We're Looking For Basic Requirements: Knowledge and skills as typically acquired through 1-3 years of systems administration experience using Microsoft Windows in a large heterogeneous environment.  In addition, the candidate must have prior experience managing Active Directory and other windows services.  Requires working knowledge of TCP/IP networking.  Also required is a strong knowledge of remote deployment.  In addition, the candidate should have prior experience using scripting languages like Powershell or Python. The candidate is expected to operate in a heterogeneous environment supporting multiple users and to help lead our Linux-windows integration efforts.  Basic user level Linux command line skills such as traversing directories, copying/renaming files, and text editing are also required. The candidate will support users working under multiple operating systems and work as a member of a team. Preferred Qualifications: Experience working with VMWare, Red Hat Linux, Network Appliance and Juniper based network equipment. Also preferable is experience with system configuration tools such as Chef/Puppet, system monitoring tools such as Nagios, and advanced knowledge of LDAP.  Preferred Windows skills include Azure/Intune. Pay Range Minimum $72,500.00, Midpoint $90,700.00, Maximum $108,900.00 Salary is based on related experience, expertise, and internal equity; generally, new hires can expect pay between the minimum and midpoint of the range. Apply Refer JOB_DESCRIPTION.SHARE.HTML CAROUSEL_PARAGRAPH JOB_DESCRIPTION.SHARE.HTML An employee in this position must complete all appropriate background checks at the time of hire, promotion, or transfer. Tufts University is an equal opportunity employer. Tufts Non-Discrimination Statement Tufts Annual Security Report On Campus Safety Human Resources Office of Equal Opportunity Accessibility Privacy © Tufts University 2026 Cookies are used on this site to assist in continually improving the candidate experience and all the interaction data we store of our visitors is anonymous. Learn more about your rights on our Privacy Policy page. Okay x"
    },
