    "https://jobs.tufts.edu/jobs/23713?lang=en-us": {
      "title": "Pre-Award Research Administrator I in Boston, Massachusetts",
      "description": "Pre-Award Research Administrator I in Boston, Massachusetts | Tufts University Skip to Main Content toggle menu CLOSE About Benefits Opportunities DEI Community Open Positions Back Pre-Award Research Administrator I JOB_DESCRIPTION.SHARE.HTML CAROUSEL_PARAGRAPH JOB_DESCRIPTION.SHARE.HTML Boston, Massachusetts Remote Research Administration 23713 mail_outline Get future jobs matching this search Login or Register Job Description Overview The Office of University Research and Innovation (OURI) supports Tufts University's research, scholarship, innovation, and entrepreneurial activities across all campuses. OURI partners with faculty, staff, students, and university leadership to advance groundbreaking research, secure external funding, ensure regulatory compliance, and translate discoveries into real-world impact. OURI provides expertise and oversight across sponsored research administration, research compliance, intellectual property management, technology commercialization, startup development, and industry partnerships. Through these efforts, OURI helps strengthen Tufts' research enterprise while supporting the university's commitment to innovation, collaboration, and academic excellence. Research Administration plays a critical role in making research possible. Working in partnership with faculty, research administrators support the business, regulatory, and compliance activities that enable groundbreaking discoveries, scholarly activity, and externally funded research. Research administration offers a rewarding career path at the intersection of research, problem-solving, and service. This role offers significant flexibility and can be performed primarily remotely, with only occasional on-campus presence as needed. What You'll Do Working under the direction of the Associate Director, Pre-Award Research Administration, you will support a portfolio of departments responsible for submitting approximately 100 sponsored proposals annually. As part of a collaborative research administration team, you will assist faculty and investigators throughout the proposal process, helping ensure compliance with sponsor requirements and university policies while supporting non-fiscal post-award activities. This role offers an opportunity to build expertise in research administration within a supportive, growth-oriented environment. Responsibilities include: Review sponsored proposals and budgets to ensure compliance with sponsor requirements and university policies. Assist with the preparation of agreements and support negotiations involving standard terms and conditions under supervision. Prepare documentation for non-fiscal post-award actions, including no-cost extensions, budget reallocations, and contract amendments. Serve as a resource to principal investigators and departmental research administrators by answering questions and providing guidance on policies and procedures. Assist with ad hoc reporting and administrative projects. Develop and maintain expertise in research administration, sponsor requirements, and university policies. Perform other duties as needed. What We're Looking For Application Instructions: To apply, please submit the following materials: 1.) Resume 2.) Cover Letter. Your cover letter should briefly describe your interest in this role, your motivation for supporting research at Tufts, and the key skills or experiences that make you a strong fit for a Pre‑Award Research Administrator I position. Basic Requirements: Knowledge and experience typically acquired by: Bachelor's degree or equivalent combination of education and experience. 0-2 years of professional experience in research administration, higher education, grants administration, compliance, finance, project coordination, or a related field. Understanding of federal research funding regulations and related compliance requirements, or the ability to learn and apply them. Proficiency with Microsoft Office applications, including Outlook, Word, Excel, and PowerPoint. Experience with, or the ability to learn, electronic research administration and grants management systems, such as Grants.gov, NIH eRA Commons, NSF Research.gov/FastLane, ProposalCentral, and other sponsor systems. Strong customer service, communication, and interpersonal skills. Strong organizational skills, attention to detail, and ability to manage multiple priorities and deadlines. Ability to work both independently and collaboratively in a fast-paced environment. Preferred Qualifications: Experience supporting sponsored research, grants administration, contracts administration, compliance, finance, higher education administration, or a related function. Knowledge of major federal sponsors and funding agencies, including NIH, NSF, DOD, DOE, or foundations. Experience working with faculty, researchers, or other professional stakeholders. Interest in building a career in research administration. Pay Range Minimum $55,600.00, Midpoint $69,500.00, Maximum $83,400.00 Salary is based on related experience, expertise, and internal equity; generally, new hires can expect pay between the minimum and midpoint of the range. Apply Refer JOB_DESCRIPTION.SHARE.HTML CAROUSEL_PARAGRAPH JOB_DESCRIPTION.SHARE.HTML An employee in this position must complete all appropriate background checks at the time of hire, promotion, or transfer. Tufts University is an equal opportunity employer. Tufts Non-Discrimination Statement Tufts Annual Security Report On Campus Safety Human Resources Office of Equal Opportunity Accessibility Privacy © Tufts University 2026 Cookies are used on this site to assist in continually improving the candidate experience and all the interaction data we store of our visitors is anonymous. Learn more about your rights on our Privacy Policy page. Okay x"
    },
