    "https://jobs.tufts.edu/jobs/23720?lang=en-us": {
      "title": "Research Tech in Boston, Massachusetts",
      "description": "Research Tech in Boston, Massachusetts | Tufts University Skip to Main Content toggle menu CLOSE About Benefits Opportunities DEI Community Open Positions Back Research Tech JOB_DESCRIPTION.SHARE.HTML CAROUSEL_PARAGRAPH JOB_DESCRIPTION.SHARE.HTML Boston, Massachusetts On-Site Research 23720 mail_outline Get future jobs matching this search Login or Register Job Description Overview *** No job summary text exists in JDX for this position *** What You'll Do Under close supervision of Principal Investigator, conducts a variety of routine experiments following established procedures and protocols, which may include performing assays, tissue culture, electrophoresis, and other laboratory techniques.  May also record test results, analyze data using basic statistics, maintain laboratory equipment and supplies, and monitor animal colonies. Conducts routine experiments following appropriate protocols and procedures to achieve results Performs techniques such as tissue culture, PCR, immunohistochemistry, electrophoresis, protein purification and others Records results and maintains accurate records of experiments Performs limited data interpretation and assists with basic statistics and analysis Maintains laboratory equipment and orders/keeps inventory of supplies Prepares stock solutions, reagents and other media Monitors animal colonies and performs husbandry, collects samples and maintains census records What We're Looking For Basic Requirements: Knowledge and experience typically acquired by: Bachelor's Degree related science The following required knowledge and skills as typically acquired by completing a Bachelor’s degree in science with up to one year laboratory experience Preferred Qualifications: Familiarity with basic laboratory techniques and procedures Pay Range Minimum $20.90, Midpoint $24.90, Maximum $28.90 Salary is based on related experience, expertise, and internal equity; generally, new hires can expect pay between the minimum and midpoint of the range. Apply Refer JOB_DESCRIPTION.SHARE.HTML CAROUSEL_PARAGRAPH JOB_DESCRIPTION.SHARE.HTML An employee in this position must complete all appropriate background checks at the time of hire, promotion, or transfer. Tufts University is an equal opportunity employer. Tufts Non-Discrimination Statement Tufts Annual Security Report On Campus Safety Human Resources Office of Equal Opportunity Accessibility Privacy © Tufts University 2026 Cookies are used on this site to assist in continually improving the candidate experience and all the interaction data we store of our visitors is anonymous. Learn more about your rights on our Privacy Policy page. Okay x"
